drain",","," the"," sound"," of"," a"," loose"," board",","," and"," a"," disagreement"," about"," whether"," a"," distant"," chimney"," belonged"," to"," the"," mill"," or"," the"," bakery","."," By"," the"," return"," journey",","," everyone"," had"," adopted"," a"," different"," theory","."," We"," ended"," at"," the"," covered"," market",","," where"," somebody"," produced"," a"," therm","os"," and"," somebody"," else"," discovered"," that"," an"," apparently"," waterproof"," map"," was"," not"," waterproof"," at"," all","."," Next"," week"," we"," will"," bring"," a"," larger"," map"," case"," and"," leave"," more"," time"," for"," the"," pumping"," house","."],"ids_available":true,"boundaries_approximate":false,"piece_format":"hex_bytes","decoded_text":"Today's walking-club log\nRoute: the canal path to the disused lock and back\nWeather: bright at the start, then a slow arrival of drizzle\n\nWe divided into two groups at the footbridge because several people wanted time to sketch the old pumping house. There was no competition to finish first. Those who walked ahead left a chalk arrow at the agreed turning point, and the rest of us caught up beside the lock keeper's cottage.\nMy notebook contains fewer distances than expected. I wrote down the pattern of reeds beside a drain, the sound of a loose board, and a disagreement about whether a distant chimney belonged to the mill or the bakery. By the return journey, everyone had adopted a different theory. We ended at the covered market, where somebody produced a thermos and somebody else discovered that an apparently waterproof map was not waterproof at all. Next week we will bring a larger map case and leave more time for the pumping house.","measurement_context":null,"character_measurement":null,"roundtrip_exact":true},{"id":"fineweb-en-0033","collection":"dataset/fineweb/en.jsonl","text":"Before a small renovation begins, we make a shared sequence of work visible to everyone involved. The painter does not need a complete account of the electrician's tools, but does need to know when a wall will be ready. The owner should not have to infer that sequence from several unrelated telephone calls.\nOur project office keeps one current schedule with a named contact for each stage. Changes are recorded with their practical effect: which visit moves, which room remains unavailable, and who needs to hear about it. This does not remove every surprise from an older building. It does make surprises easier to distinguish from information that somebody forgot to pass along. We also identify pauses during which no work is planned, so that an empty room is not automatically mistaken for an abandoned job. A reliable plan is less like a prediction that nothing will change and more like an arrangement for explaining what a change means when it occurs.","token_ids":[10438,264,2678,50555,12302,11,584,1304,264,6222,8668,315,990,9621,311,5127,6532,13,578,30581,1587,539,1205,264,4686,2759,315,279,9249,1122,596,7526,11,719,1587,1205,311,1440,994,264,7147,690,387,5644,13,578,6506,1288,539,617,311,24499,430,8668,505,3892,46305,21186,6880,627,8140,2447,5274,13912,832,1510,9899,449,264,7086,3729,369,1855,6566,13,29240,527,12715,449,872,15325,2515,25,902,4034,11031,11,902,3130,8625,36087,11,323,889,3966,311,6865,922,433,13,1115,1587,539,4148,1475,13051,505,459,9191,4857,13,1102,1587,1304,46540,8831,311,33137,505,2038,430,18570,29695,311,1522,3235,13,1226,1101,10765,86932,2391,902,912,990,374,13205,11,779,430,459,4384,3130,374,539,9651,37104,369,459,23838,2683,13,362,15062,3197,374,2753,1093,264,20212,430,4400,690,2349,323,810,1093,459,27204,369,26073,1148,264,2349,3445,994,433,13980,13],"tokens":["4265666f7265","2061","20736d616c6c","2072656e6f766174696f6e","20626567696e73","2c","207765","206d616b65","2061","20736861726564","2073657175656e6365","206f66","20776f726b","2076697369626c65","20746f","2065766572796f6e65","20696e766f6c766564","2e","20546865","207061696e746572","20646f6573","206e6f74","206e656