s","."," Whoever"," did"," it"," clearly"," wanted"," the"," repair"," to"," last",","," but"," also"," wanted"," the"," next"," person"," to"," enjoy"," finding"," it",".\n\n","I"," was"," going"," to"," replace"," the"," lining","."," Now"," I","'m"," making"," a"," little"," patch"," beside"," the"," old"," one"," and"," leaving"," that"," work"," visible","."," An"," accidental"," collaboration"," across"," an"," unknown"," number"," of"," years","."," �","�","�","\n\n","Reply",":"," Could"," you"," post"," a"," close","-up"," without"," the"," shop"," label","?"," I","'d"," love"," to"," see"," the"," stitch"," pattern",".\n\n","Done",","," in"," the"," second"," image","."," Description",":"," parallel"," rows"," of"," blue"," stitches"," around"," a"," small"," brown"," patch",","," with"," one"," yellow"," thread"," tying"," off"," the"," corner","."," My"," contribution"," is"," the"," less"," elegant"," green"," square"," below"," it",".\n\n","Please"," don","'t"," be"," intimidated"," by"," the"," neat","ness"," of"," the"," original","."," The"," jacket"," was"," wearable"," with"," the"," hole",";"," it"," is"," wearable"," with"," my"," w","obb","ly"," repair","."," Clothes"," aren","'t"," an"," exam","."," I","'m"," mostly"," delighted"," to"," have"," found"," something"," useful"," that"," also"," contains"," a"," small"," mystery",".\n\n","#","Visible","M","ending"," #","Second","Hand"],"ids_available":true,"boundaries_approximate":false,"piece_format":"hex_bytes","decoded_text":"Bought a second-hand jacket with a spectacular repair inside the lining. Tiny, even stitches in three different colours. Whoever did it clearly wanted the repair to last, but also wanted the next person to enjoy finding it.\n\nI was going to replace the lining. Now I'm making a little patch beside the old one and leaving that work visible. An accidental collaboration across an unknown number of years. 🧵\n\nReply: Could you post a close-up without the shop label? I'd love to see the stitch pattern.\n\nDone, in the second image. Description: parallel rows of blue stitches around a small brown patch, with one yellow thread tying off the corner. My contribution is the less elegant green square below it.\n\nPlease don't be intimidated by the neatness of the original. The jacket was wearable with the hole; it is wearable with my wobbly repair. Clothes aren't an exam. I'm mostly delighted to have found something useful that also contains a small mystery.\n\n#VisibleMending #SecondHand","measurement_context":null,"character_measurement":null,"roundtrip_exact":true},{"id":"sns-ja-0019","collection":"dataset/sns/ja.jsonl","text":"人物を描く練習で、今日は手ではなく「何を持っているか」から考えた。\n熱いマグ、重い袋、落としたくない卵。同じ指の数でも、力の入る場所が全然違う。\n\n自分でポーズを取って撮った写真、顔の真剣さが必要以上で笑ってしまった。資料として使う部分だけ切り出すつもりだったのに、その必死な表情まで絵に入りそう。\n\n返信：卵は本物？\n→空の殻に紙を詰めたものです。部屋で割る未来が見えたので、先に対策しました🥚\n\n一枚を仕上げるより、違いを三つ見つけて終わる日があってもいい。今日のノートには、指の線より「親指は思ったより低い」といった文字の方が多い。しばらくしたらまた同じ題材を描き、自分がどこを見るようになったか比べてみます。","token_ids":[17792,53953,30512,21441,237,47884,163,115,112,163,123,240,16556,5486,37271,9080,15682,46034,77181,26854,47884,13177,99849,30512,69978,76947,16995,30369,32149,10646,55031,78698,58942,28713,9174,163,228,109,16995,68759,41758,5486,30358,16995,87743,233,5486,81180,121,19732,56051,47884,26854,16995,11239,113,1811,42016,100204,64467,16144,9039,72661,5486,48634,16144,17701,30369,75267,32938,29295,37087,61994,30250,243,30297,3490,37026,17620,16556,89154,38248,118,30512,18655,76947,58843,106,42891,28713,62543,89151,5486,14167,242,16144,89151,21403,96,30813,29295,59614,31634,71689,16556,49838,76947,15024,17129,42891,28713,1811,83812,229,42506,19732,39926,33655,30297,34048,17620,36785,76622,6701,229,31431,20834,17663,59739,32977,31431,36785,42891,28713,16144,20230,5486,58426,59614,15722,119,26854,21405,40474,17129,16556,58254,113,20230,17701,31431,27929,30297,3490,10287,242,22023,5232,11239,113,15682,22656,53953,95532,52118,35894,16144,36149,119,20230,27869,247,30512,50520,108,62004,28713,32977,16144,386